{"title":"Sharma Math Exam 2026 Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sharma_Math_Exam_2026_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b56d32444d8efd65eb0cb6c01f8ac72c32587e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are real numbers that satisfy the system of equations below.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9863eb481b1bbe61e71bb1e23723c850c6e5dbd0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{cases} \\tan(x) \\cdot \\tan(y) &amp;= \\frac{1}{3}\\\\ \\tan(x) \\cdot \\tan(z) &amp;= \\frac{1}{5}\\\\ \\tan(y) \\cdot \\tan(z) &amp;= \\frac{1}{7} \\end{cases}\\]\" width=\"171\" height=\"74\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b28bf6c0e1552aa67bf0993942598b5e6e2359cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(2x + 2y + 2z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"141\" height=\"20\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/888fed89e19182447f85b3cb6676548a49395284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"27\" height=\"34\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime integers. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/1/c91f584215242319c296604fac17fd4c0567c508.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{m + n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"21\" /> rounded to the nearest hundredth?\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/d/a7dc377a91146d081efc1f4ba0c4cd157fe96232.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 16.00 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 17.00 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 18.00 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 22.63 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 25.46$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"517\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sharma_Math_Exam_2026_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0ebc8088e2c58d4fff8d8e42b6a8b88947e9f8fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(x) = a,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/a/51a2b58442bf211a07b4c5bbcd5c7f32a434527b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(y) = b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/e/0eeec0a42c034f4b498bb90bd8624916a6e33142.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(z) = c.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/238c74adffae4fa79c162b3f0c3b9fcf4361a10a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\cdot b \\cdot c = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 7}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{105}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"221\" height=\"43\" />\nDivide the first two equations in the system to get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/e/eeebdf167bc3d5bd848a01de7e491a4a400505d3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{b}{c} = \\frac{5}{3} \\implies b = \\frac{5}{3} \\cdot c\\]\" width=\"163\" height=\"38\" />\nPlug <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> in for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> in the third equation: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/c/d1c11af59fe7bd753ce1a4bcb32766cf229d21ea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{5}{3} \\cdot c^2 = \\frac{1}{7} \\implies c = \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{35}} = \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{105}}.\\]\" width=\"272\" height=\"46\" />\nThen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a846290115e90c3441781fe235828798adf7ea2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{105}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"80\" height=\"43\" />. From the first equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/3/3936e1dd2ab5fdad0a331276345d0ca94b03266f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{1}{3b} \\implies a = \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{105}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"191\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Start by finding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/5/96576a4e162157ba8baf170281c62d8ac29331c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(x + y + z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" /> then solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b28bf6c0e1552aa67bf0993942598b5e6e2359cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(2x + 2y + 2z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"141\" height=\"20\" /> from there. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/9/f39af86771b56c7e2823db629c6e14485d04cfc6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan(x + y + z) = \\tan((x + y) + z) = \\frac{\\tan(x + y) + c}{1 - \\tan(x+y) \\cdot c}\\]\" width=\"428\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/290183d9545de83151b1aba2d2352c08f4993040.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan(x + y) = \\frac{a + b}{1 - ab}\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"37\" />\nPlugging this into our expression for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/5/96576a4e162157ba8baf170281c62d8ac29331c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(x + y + z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/2/f72217917adc6c940043c6b68cfa9af404d21875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(x + y + z) = \\frac{a + b + c - abc}{1 - (ab + ac + bc)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"285\" height=\"44\" />\nSubstitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94d66a4eaa45e6859e3df49470c54a33253b82dd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan(x + y + z) = \\frac{\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{105}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{105}}}{1 - (\\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{5} + \\frac{1}{7})} = \\frac{735}{17\\sqrt{105}}\\]\" width=\"351\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>Now, recall that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/b/8dbe0c75c5a94cd35073b16bb869115a26eafbba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan^2{x} = \\frac{\\sin^2{x}}{\\cos^2{x}} = \\frac{1 - \\cos^2x}{\\cos^2x} \\implies \\cos^2{x} = \\frac{\\cos{2x} + 1}{2} = \\frac{1}{\\tan^2{x} + 1} \\implies \\cos{2x} = \\frac{1 - \\tan^2(x)}{1 + \\tan^2(x)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"754\" height=\"47\" />\nSo we have: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/4/004eacf39acad15d9ec510ccbc7d791bec295dee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos{2(x + y + z)} = \\frac{1 - (\\frac{735}{17\\sqrt{105}})^2}{1 + (\\frac{735}{17\\sqrt{105}})^2} = \\frac{1 - \\frac{5145}{289}}{1 + \\frac{5145}{289}} = \\frac{-4856}{5434} = \\frac{-2428}{2717}.\\]\" width=\"504\" height=\"52\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/9/a892838a4f128673ae775b48d6fe3bcd531c4285.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{-2428 + 2717} = \\sqrt{289} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }17.00}.\\]\" width=\"305\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018041114\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.029 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 119/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6786/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36068:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018041114 and revision id 281998. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}